// The grant names one host, and the module asks for a different *name* for the
// same machine. `localhost` resolves to `127.0.0.1`, but the check matches the
// host as the code wrote it, `getaddrinfo` runs only after the check, so this
// is denied rather than silently allowed. That is the design rule S3 records:
// a grant for `example.com` does not cover `93.184.216.34`, and a grant for
// `127.0.0.1` does not cover `localhost`.
impl "util" caps(net = ["127.0.0.1:*"])

fun main() {
    print(util.connect_by_another_name())
}
